# Backend Rules (`apps/api`)

Stack: NestJS, Better Auth (Bearer), Drizzle (`@elynd/db`), Zod (`@elynd/shared` / nestjs-zod), Vitest.

Prefer [`.trellis/spec/api/backend/`](../../.trellis/spec/api/backend/index.md) and official Nest / Better Auth docs over inventing new structure.

## TypeScript

- Extend `@elynd/tsconfig/nest.json`
- Keep `outDir` / `rootDir` / `include` / `types` local
- **Imports (N1):** use relative NodeNext imports with `.js` suffixes inside the API. Do **not** enable `@/` path aliases in emitted code until a Nest emit rewrite (e.g. `tsc-alias`) is added

## Layout

- Feature modules under `src/api/<feature>/` or `src/auth/`
- Cross-cutting code in `src/common/` (guards, pipes, filters, decorators)
- Global providers in `src/global/`
- Lazy Better Auth via `getAuthInstance()` — never eager-init at import time

## Controllers / services

- Thin controllers: validate + map HTTP; business rules in injectable services
- Auth application logic goes through `AuthApplicationService` + `AuthClientPort` (mock the port in unit tests)
- Do not use Adonis-style Access Token auth on the Nest path

## Validation & OpenAPI

- Prefer shared Zod schemas from `@elynd/shared/schemas`
- Use project Zod validation pipe / Swagger helpers already in `src/common`

## Env

Required auth-related keys: `DATABASE_URI`, `AUTH_SECRET`, `BETTER_AUTH_URL`, `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` (see `auth-env.schema.ts`).

## Lint

Use `@elynd/eslint-config/nest` via local `eslint.config.mjs`.
